WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.297 --> 00:00:06.173
What are you doing here?

00:00:06.632 --> 00:00:07.299
Let me in.

00:00:07.633 --> 00:00:11.261
Alex, because she
is Mitch’s equal,

00:00:11.261 --> 00:00:13.680
she is a white
woman of privilege,

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:16.391
she has experienced
a certain kind of Mitch

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:20.270
and so, she’s really 
trying to wrestle with

00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:23.523
her experience of Mitch and who
she knows him to be with

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:25.400
other women’s 
experiences of him.

00:00:25.734 --> 00:00:26.902
I wanna be better!

00:00:26.902 --> 00:00:28.570
I wanna be a
better person, please!

00:00:29.363 --> 00:00:31.156
Just no,
seriously Alex!

00:00:32.407 --> 00:00:35.744
I just, I want
to be a good person!

00:00:36.036 --> 00:00:37.204
As human beings

00:00:37.204 --> 00:00:40.791
we are fallible, we are
capable of horrible things.

00:00:40.791 --> 00:00:42.793
We are capable of
wonderful things.

00:00:42.793 --> 00:00:47.172
And we don’t make
enough room in this moment

00:00:47.714 --> 00:00:49.132
for contrition,

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:53.512
to be able to say sorry,
to mean it, to move on.

00:00:53.762 --> 00:00:56.431
We’re dealing with it in the
best way we can on the show

00:00:56.431 --> 00:00:57.933
cause I think it’s
really important

00:00:57.933 --> 00:00:59.268
cause that is the big question.

00:00:59.268 --> 00:01:01.144
Is there redemption for anyone?

00:01:01.645 --> 00:01:04.106
And he’s trying
to understand.

00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:06.275
He really wants to do better.

00:01:06.608 --> 00:01:08.527
It’s just time for me to go,
we were quarantining.

00:01:08.527 --> 00:01:11.321
I know that you don’t 
actually want to leave,

00:01:11.321 --> 00:01:13.907
so could we just
stop with the pretending?

00:01:13.907 --> 00:01:14.741
Valeria Golino

00:01:15.242 --> 00:01:18.704
Ugh! She’s so incredible.
She’s one of the

00:01:18.704 --> 00:01:22.749
most free, wonderful
ators I’ve ever worked with.

00:01:22.749 --> 00:01:25.085
She’s just not
afraid of anything

00:01:25.335 --> 00:01:27.671
and her character represents

00:01:27.671 --> 00:01:30.382
someone who
has no judgement on Mitch

00:01:30.382 --> 00:01:31.675
Yes he has a past

00:01:31.675 --> 00:01:33.552
but she accepts him
for who he is.

00:01:33.802 --> 00:01:36.430
Valeria understood it all
immediately,

00:01:36.471 --> 00:01:39.474
ya know. And there’s
an irreverence to her,

00:01:39.975 --> 00:01:44.980
and a kind of daring to her as a
performer that Paola needed

00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:46.481
and we saw it right away.

00:01:46.481 --> 00:01:49.693
[whispering]
[laughing]

00:01:49.693 --> 00:01:52.612
I’m on a mission, I’m on a
mission, I’m on a mission!

00:01:53.697 --> 00:01:55.324
Our writers always knew

00:01:55.324 --> 00:01:57.409
that Mitch would pass
away this season.

00:01:57.409 --> 00:01:59.953
One of the things that we
talked about is how,

00:01:59.953 --> 00:02:03.582
when someone passes
the story about them can shift.

00:02:03.582 --> 00:02:06.418
And it was very interesting and
rich territory to explore

00:02:06.752 --> 00:02:09.880
how people would feel not just
about Mitch when he was living

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:11.798
but how they would feel
about him when he passed.

00:02:11.798 --> 00:02:12.591
We ask

00:02:13.216 --> 00:02:16.136
who we are as people when
we’ve done horrible things.

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:19.139
Are we still a human being,
or are we a monster?

00:02:19.473 --> 00:02:20.640
That’s not for us to answer.

00:02:21.224 --> 00:02:22.559
It’s for the audience to answer.

